{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e67603ac-41cf-4242-b612-3e3b3aec794b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdd97dca26f1e03c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E001.md","content":"# Structured Kueue workload status model with eviction-reason separation and message overrides\n\n## Description\n\nRebuilds the workbench workload status derivation in the odh-dashboard frontend to be\nstate-driven from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses, replacing the current\nevent-driven model that conflates all Evicted conditions as \"Preempted\" and relies on\nwildcard/substring matching of events. Delivers accurate, human-readable scheduling status\nfor Kueue-managed workbenches: distinct eviction reasons, Requeued retry state, full\ncondition coverage with human-friendly message overrides and a raw-message fallback.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Correct the `WorkloadCondition` type union in `k8sTypes.ts`: remove the invalid `'Failed'`\n  entry (failure is expressed as `Finished` with reason `Failed`) and include `QuotaReserved`,\n  `Admitted`, `PodsReady`, `Finished`, `Evicted`, `Preempted`, `Requeued`,\n  `BlockedOnPreemptionGates`, `DeactivationTarget`.\n- Implement a structured, extensible status derivation model that computes workbench status\n  from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses rather than hardcoded progress\n  steps and wildcard/substring event matching. Unknown condition types must flow through\n  the model without breaking existing status logic.\n- Distinguish \"Preempted\" (higher-priority workload took resources) from \"Evicted\" (admin\n  action, timeout, or other reasons) in the status label and variant. Handle the full set\n  of eviction reasons: Preempted, PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped,\n  LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded.\n- Surface the Requeued state: when a workload is evicted and waiting to re-enter the queue,\n  display retry count and next retry time computed from `requeueState` (including\n  `requeueState.requeueAt`).\n- Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, and\n  surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n- Provide a human-friendly message override lookup table for known condition/reason\n  combinations, with reasonable placeholder defaults. The fallback for any unrecognized\n  condition/reason combination is always the raw Kueue condition `.message` field — never\n  a blank state.\n- All K8s API calls go through the `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy with the logged-in user's\n  token; workload-to-notebook matching continues to use `buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()`\n  in `api/k8s/workloads.ts`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace where a workbench has been evicted due to\n  `ClusterQueueStopped`, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays\n  \"Evicted\" with reason \"Queue stopped by administrator\" — NOT \"Preempted\", measured by the\n  status label text and variant differing from the Preempted state.\n- Given a workbench has been evicted and the Workload CR has a `Requeued` condition with\n  `requeueState.requeueAt` set, when the user views the workbench status, then the status\n  displays retry information including next retry time and attempt count, measured by the\n  status text including the computed retry time from `requeueState`.\n- Given a workbench's Workload CR has a condition type or reason not recognized by the\n  dashboard's status model, when the workbench status is rendered, then the raw Kueue\n  condition message is displayed rather than a blank state, measured by the status text\n  containing the Workload CR's condition `.message` field content.\n- Given a Workload CR containing condition types not yet in the dashboard's\n  `WorkloadCondition` type union, when status is rendered, then the unknown condition is\n  shown with raw message text and never silently dropped, measured by rendering a workload\n  with a synthetic unknown condition type.\n- Given a cluster where Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not Kueue-managed, when\n  the user views workbench status, then existing workbench status behavior is unchanged,\n  measured by regression against current status display for non-Kueue workloads.\n- The status model is implemented as a structured derivation from Workload CR conditions\n  rather than wildcard/substring matching of events, measured by code review confirming no\n  event-substring matching remains in the status derivation path and by unit tests covering\n  each condition type in the type union.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons in the workbench status display.\n- HLR-2 (P0): Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState`.\n- HLR-5 (P0): Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions with\n  human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback (placeholder overrides;\n  final reviewed microcopy is delivered by the UX content workstream).\n- HLR-10 (P2): Structured, extensible status derivation model replacing wildcard/substring\n  event matching.\n- HLR-11 (P2): Status message granularity — WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck\n  pending/retry states.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40410,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a60dde69fe10feb4","agent_id":"a4bc18f31254a1faa","session_id":"c707f99e-2a7a-41d1-b409-ac9a210055ae","uuid":"298f3f68-e7e8-4709-9ee5-c5459729d178","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:51:50.298Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
