{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b4f1d1ae-d4c5-4fed-813f-d4f3671ddc10","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28711da0b008299","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E003.md","content":"# Kueue Visibility API queue-position integration with graceful RBAC degradation\n\n## Description\n\nIntegrates Kueue's Visibility API into the odh-dashboard workbenches overview so users can\nsee a pending workbench's position in its queue. Queue position is not a field on the\nWorkload object — it is served by Kueue's aggregated API server at API group\n`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io` via `PendingWorkload` resources, exposed as subresources on\nqueues. Display is supplementary and must degrade silently when the user's RBAC does not\npermit reading it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Fetch queue position for pending workloads via the LocalQueue `pendingworkloads`\n  subresource: `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`,\n  reading `positionInLocalQueue` (and `positionInClusterQueue` where available) from the\n  `PendingWorkloadsSummary`.\n- Display the position number for workbenches in QueuingPending state in the workbenches\n  overview, alongside the scheduling status.\n- Graceful degradation on 403: a 403 on the Visibility API must fail silently — position\n  info is omitted with no error surfaced to the user. Reuse the existing\n  `getGenericErrorCode` pattern from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx`.\n- All calls go through the `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy with the logged-in user's token;\n  RBAC comes from Kueue's `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` ClusterRole aggregated to\n  `batch-user`, `view`, `admin`, and `edit` roles.\n- Only factual position data is displayed — no estimated wait-time prediction (Kueue does\n  not provide it natively).\n- Validate in a representative RHOAI cluster whether data scientists actually hold role\n  bindings that aggregate the viewer role, and record the result so the amount of position\n  UI polish can be scoped (user-facing vs. effectively admin-only).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has `batch-user` RBAC\n  to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position\n  is displayed (position in local queue), measured by the position number being present and\n  matching the value from the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT have RBAC to\n  the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is\n  silently omitted with no error displayed, measured by the absence of both position data\n  and error indicators.\n- Given a default RHOAI cluster with RHBoK, when the RBAC validation check is performed,\n  then it is documented whether data scientists' default role bindings aggregate the\n  `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`, and the position UI polish scope is recorded\n  accordingly, measured by a written finding attached to this epic's completion.\n- The UI remains responsive with the Visibility API integration, measured by the workbenches\n  overview rendering without position-fetch requests blocking initial paint (supplementary\n  data loads asynchronously).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1): Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display\n  (`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource\n  on LocalQueue — gracefully degrade on 403.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42632,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a60dde69fe10feb4","agent_id":"a4bc18f31254a1faa","session_id":"c707f99e-2a7a-41d1-b409-ac9a210055ae","uuid":"911