{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-de948f6b-fdd1-419d-a29e-b896bde6dd95","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74700ec297eb562","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E004.md","content":"# HardwareProfile queue-name validation, GitOps popover fallback, and dropdown explanation\n\n## Description\n\nHardens the HardwareProfile-related surfaces in the odh-dashboard for Kueue-managed\nprojects: validates LocalQueue names in the admin form, handles GitOps-managed notebooks\nthat carry the queue label directly (with no matching HardwareProfile) in the HP details\npopover, and explains why only queue-enabled profiles appear in the workbench creation\ndropdown.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **LocalQueue name validation (HardwareProfile admin form):** validate the LocalQueue name\n  field against `k8sNameRegex` (`/^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$/`). Existence of the queue\n  cannot be validated at HP creation time because HardwareProfiles are cluster-scoped while\n  LocalQueues are namespace-scoped — format validation only.\n- **Workbench creation warning for missing LocalQueue:** at workbench creation time, if the\n  specified local queue does not exist in the target namespace, display a warning — NOT an\n  error. The admin may have intended the LQ to be created later or delivered via GitOps;\n  these are eventually consistent systems and Kueue itself reports the error via the\n  Workload's conditions if the queue truly doesn't exist. The warning must be dismissible\n  and must not block creation.\n- **HP details popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks:** when a notebook has\n  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` applied directly via GitOps (no HardwareProfile match), the\n  HP details popover falls back to reading the queue label from the notebook's own labels,\n  resolving the cluster queue name from the project's LocalQueue list, and indicating the\n  source: \"Queue: my-queue (applied directly)\" vs. \"Queue: my-queue (via hardware profile)\".\n- **HP dropdown explanation:** keep strict filtering (only queue-based HPs shown in\n  Kueue-managed namespaces) but add an explicit info indicator — info icon or tooltip —\n  explaining \"Only queue-enabled hardware profiles are shown because this project uses\n  queue-based scheduling.\" Be opinionated, but tell users we are being opinionated.\n- All changes are additive and conditional on the namespace being Kueue-managed; existing\n  behavior in non-Kueue namespaces is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an admin is creating a HardwareProfile and enters an invalid LocalQueue name\n  (e.g., contains uppercase or spaces), when the form validates, then a validation error is\n  shown for the LocalQueue name field, measured by the form displaying an inline error\n  referencing the Kubernetes name format.\n- Given a workbench is being created with a HardwareProfile referencing a LocalQueue that\n  does not exist in the target namespace, when the creation form is submitted, then a\n  warning (not error) is displayed indicating the local queue was not found, measured by\n  the warning being dismissible and not blocking workbench creation.\n- Given a GitOps-managed workbench with `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label applied directly\n  (no matching HardwareProfile), when the user opens the HardwareProfile details popover,\n  then the popover displays the queue name with indication it was applied directly (not via\n  hardware profile), measured by the popover text including the queue name and a source\n  indicator.\n- Given a workbench is in a Kueue-managed namespace and the user opens the workbench\n  creation form, when the HardwareProfile dropdown renders with only queue-enabled profiles,\n  then an info indicator explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown, measured by\n  the presence of a tooltip or info icon adjacent to the dropdown.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): Fix HardwareProfile details popover for GitOps-managed notebooks — read queue\n  label directly when no HP match exists, indicate source.\n- HLR-8 (P1): Add `k8sNameRegex` validation to LocalQueue name field in HardwareProfile\n  admin form (including the non-blocking missing-queue warning at workbench creation time).\n- HLR-9 (P1): Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only queue-enabled\n  profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43559,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a60dde69fe10feb4","agent_id":"a4bc18f31254a1faa","session_id":"c707f99e-2a7a-41d1-b409-ac9a210055ae","uuid":"fc4a76c1-7979-4399-aeb9-bd8e85388ecb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:52:30.627Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002 into epics"}
