*Delivery mechanism:** hand finalized copy and treatments to the dashboard team (or land\n  them directly in the override table and component styles in the odh-dashboard frontend).\n- Constraint: the fallback behavior — raw Kueue condition message displayed when no\n  override exists — is an engineering invariant and not changed by this work; content\n  review covers the override table entries only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Final microcopy exists for every known condition/reason combination in the status message\n  override table, reviewed with the Content team, measured by a completed review record for\n  the full override table delivered against the implemented condition set.\n- The final visual treatment and copy for the positive Kueue indicator on the project\n  details page is specified and replaces the placeholder treatment, measured by the\n  specification delivered (RHOAIUX-7470) and the placeholder replacement tracked to done.\n- The final visual treatment and copy for the non-Kueue workload anomaly indicator is\n  specified and replaces the placeholder treatment, measured by the specification delivered\n  and the placeholder replacement tracked to done.\n- The finalized content is technically reviewed against the implemented status model to\n  confirm every override entry maps to a real condition/reason combination, measured by a\n  review sign-off noting any unmapped entries as defects.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P0, content refinement): human-friendly message overrides for Kueue\n  condition/reason combinations — final reviewed microcopy replacing engineering\n  placeholder defaults.\n- HLR-3 (P0, visual treatment): positive Kueue indicator on project details page — final\n  form and copy (RHOAIUX-7470).\n- HLR-4 (P0, visual treatment): anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads — final form and\n  copy.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44641,"output_tokens":0},"context_manag