{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84e864c71a9ea6fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Kueue management indicators: positive project indicator and non-Kueue workload\n4\t  anomaly indicator'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard UI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Kueue management indicators: positive project indicator and non-Kueue workload anomaly indicator\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAdds conditional Kueue visibility indicators to the odh-dashboard frontend so users know\n35\twhen their project uses queue-based scheduling. Two indicators: a positive indicator on\n36\tthe project details page for Kueue-managed namespaces, and an anomaly indicator on\n37\tindividual workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue even though their namespace is\n38\tKueue-managed (the hybrid GitOps + dashboard case).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- **Positive Kueue indicator (project details page):** when the namespace has the\n43\t  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label, display an indicator stating that this project\n44\t  uses queue-based scheduling. Ship with a placeholder visual treatment (info banner, badge,\n45\t  or label) and placeholder copy; the final treatment and wording are a UX decision\n46\t  (RHOAIUX-7470) delivered by the UX content workstream.\n47\t- **Anomaly indicator (workbenches overview):** in a Kueue-managed namespace, flag only the\n48\t  anomaly — workbenches that do NOT carry the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via\n49\t  GitOps or CLI, bypassing Kueue) get a visual indicator that they are not managed by Kueue.\n50\t  Do NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every workload in a Kueue-managed namespace — that is\n51\t  redundant in the steady state.\n52\t- All indicators are purely additive and conditional: absent when the namespace is not\n53\t  Kueue-managed, with existing workbench behavior unchanged.\n54\t- Namespace labels are read through the `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy with the logged-in\n55\t  user's token, subject to the user's RBAC permissions.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a\n60\t  positive indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured\n61\t  by the indicator element being present in the DOM when the namespace label\n62\t  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists and absent when it does not.\n63\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the\n64\t  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment),\n65\t  when the user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a\n66\t  visual indicator that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being\n67\t  present only on non-Kueue workbenches and absent on Kueue-managed workbenches.\n68\t- Given a namespace without the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label, when the user views\n69\t  the project details page and workbenches overview, then neither indicator appears and\n70\t  existing behavior is unchanged, measured by DOM absence of both indicator elements.\n71\t- The positive indicator ships with placeholder visual treatment and copy that is clearly\n72\t  identifiable for later replacement, measured by the placeholder being tracked for the\n73\t  UX deliverable (RHOAIUX-7470) replacement.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-3 (P0): Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has\n78\t  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n79\t- HLR-4 (P0): Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT\n80\t  managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af1f64e3a9a94d43","agent_id":"abdf71e3adbd33bbb","session_id":"c707f99e-2a7a-41d1-b409-ac9a210055ae","uuid":"b08f4c94-2088-4eea-a36a-b4c82b2a0e52","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:54:59.861Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84e864c71a9ea6fd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
