r rewritten doc topics), or a strategy with `Documentation Support: Yes`, warrants a separate epic.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/skills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:118:5. `repo-onboarding` → `konflux-onboarding` always serial (pipeline needs repo)\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/skills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:121:8. `license-validation` ∥ `konflux-onboarding` parallel (config doesn't depend on specific deps)\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/skills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:123:10. `konflux-onboarding` ∥ general implementation parallel (config independent of code; AC gates first execution). **Add NO blocking edge in either direction.** It is tempting to make the general implementation depend on `konflux-onboarding` (\"the code needs a build pipeline first\") — do not. That coupling is enforced by the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC on the general implementation epic, never by a DAG dependency. A `konflux-onboarding → general` edge serializes work that must run in parallel and is a rule violation.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/skills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:124:11. `docs-authoring` blocked by ALL Implementation epics in strategy (always last; docs describe what was built). These edges do not trigger priority inheritance — see Step 4 `docs-authoring` priority exception.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-bdbclfxb/skills/epic-decompose/prompts/decompose-agent.md:128:13. Implementation producing artifact another epic's code builds against (API, CRD, library) → consuming Implementation serial. Does NOT apply to configuration references (image digests, endpoint URLs) — those are AC gates. **In particular, an image digest / SHA consumed by OLM