{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1c2dd68870e06e2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E005\n3\ttitle: Kueue status message microcopy and indicator visual treatment (RHOAIUX-7470)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: UXD\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8002-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 0\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Kueue status message microcopy and indicator visual treatment (RHOAIUX-7470)\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tDelivers the UX design and content workstream for Kueue scheduling visibility\n36\t(RHOAIUX-7470): finalized human-readable status message microcopy for known Kueue\n37\tcondition/reason combinations, the visual treatment for the positive Kueue indicator on\n38\tthe project details page, and the visual treatment for the non-Kueue workload anomaly\n39\tindicator. This work replaces the placeholder defaults and treatments that engineering\n40\tships with, and is deliberately non-blocking for development.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- **Status message override content:** author the final human-friendly message wording for\n45\t  the known Kueue condition/reason combinations surfaced by the workbench status display\n46\t  (eviction reasons including Preempted, PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck,\n47\t  ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures,\n48\t  MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded; Requeued retry state; WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart;\n49\t  AdmissionCheck pending/retry). Content is reviewed with the Content team\n50\t  (microcopy) and replaces the engineering placeholder defaults in the override lookup\n51\t  table.\n52\t- **Positive Kueue indicator treatment:** decide and specify the final form of the project\n53\t  details page indicator (info banner vs. badge vs. label) for namespaces labeled\n54\t  `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`, including final copy.\n55\t- **Anomaly indicator treatment:** specify the visual treatment and copy for the indicator\n56\t  shown on workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces that are missing the\n57\t  `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label.\n58\t- **Delivery mechanism:** hand finalized copy and treatments to the dashboard team (or land\n59\t  them directly in the override table and component styles in the odh-dashboard frontend).\n60\t- Constraint: the fallback behavior — raw Kueue condition message displayed when no\n61\t  override exists — is an engineering invariant and not changed by this work; content\n62\t  review covers the override table entries only.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- Final microcopy exists for every known condition/reason combination in the status message\n67\t  override table, reviewed with the Content team, measured by a completed review record for\n68\t  the full override table delivered against the implemented condition set.\n69\t- The final visual treatment and copy for the positive Kueue indicator on the project\n70\t  details page is specified and replaces the placeholder treatment, measured by the\n71\t  specification delivered (RHOAIUX-7470) and the placeholder replacement tracked to done.\n72\t- The final visual treatment and copy for the non-Kueue workload anomaly indicator is\n73\t  specified and replaces the placeholder treatment, measured by the specification delivered\n74\t  and the placeholder replacement tracked to done.\n75\t- The finalized content is technically reviewed against the implemented status model to\n76\t  confirm every override entry maps to a real condition/reason combination, measured by a\n77\t  review sign-off noting any unmapped entries as defects.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- HLR-5 (P0, content refinement): human-friendly message overrides for Kueue\n82\t  condition/reason combinations — final reviewed microcopy replacing engineering\n83\t  placeholder defaults.\n84\t- HLR-3 (P0, visual treatment): positive Kueue indicator on project details page — final\n85\t  form and copy (RHOAIUX-7470).\n86\t- HLR-4 (P0, visual treatment): anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads — final form and\n87\t  copy.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a0f5f8d63ce7094","agent_id":"a27a0f8da6f907826","session_id":"c707f99e-2a7a-41d1-b409-ac9a210055ae","uuid":"fa83e1f2-388d-40b0-bfe8-54416df0e592","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:00:36.709Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1c2dd68870e06e2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
